# Development Workflow

Use this repo's Matt Pocock engineering skills (see `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/skills/`). Prefer those over inventing a parallel process.

## Feature Implementation Workflow

### 0. Research & Reuse (MANDATORY before any new implementation)

- Search the codebase and existing patterns first
- Check primary vendor docs for APIs in use (Next.js, shadcn, tRPC, Supabase, TanStack Form, Zod, GSAP, nuqs)
- Search package registries before writing utility code — prefer battle-tested libraries
- Prefer adopting or porting a proven approach over writing net-new code when it meets the requirement

### 1. Plan First

- Sharpen with `/grill-with-docs` or `/grill-me` when the idea is still soft
- Multi-session work → `/to-spec` then `/to-tickets` (tickets partitioned into **plans** sized for one `/implement` run)
- Huge foggy efforts → `/wayfinder` first, then hand off to `/to-spec`

### 2. TDD Approach

- `/implement` drives `/tdd` at pre-agreed seams
- Write tests first (RED) → implement (GREEN) → refactor
- Run typecheck regularly; full suite once at the end of the plan

### 3. Code Review

- `/code-review` after the plan's work lands
- Address CRITICAL and HIGH issues before considering the plan done

### 4. Commit

- Commit on the current branch when the plan (or agreed slice) is done
- Prefer concise messages focused on why
- Never commit secrets (`.env.local`, service role keys)

### 5. Pre-Review Checks

- `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, and `pnpm build` (or CI equivalents) pass
- Resolve merge conflicts; keep the branch up to date with the target
